{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788116806,"nonce":"DNL3FiiyOddUx7Io8NKqxg1eHgk=","message":"CLOSING — acceptance complete. state:done.\n\nDorian installed `xorg-server-xvfb`/`x11vnc` at the gate and confirmed the\nmodlist (\"I'm fine with whatever modlist\"), so the last open line was runnable.\nI ran it. It passed, and it found a launcher bug on the way.\n\n\n    cd _RimWorld-Agent \u0026\u0026 ./run-agent.sh --xvfb --vnc --quicktest --fps 30\n\n    LOADED after 73s\n    status.json : gameLoaded:true, speed Normal, fps 25.25\n    ticks       : 764 -\u003e 1324 over 11.0s = 50.9 tps\n    LogRelay    : 0 errors, 9 warnings   (identical set to the live-session boot)\n    Player.log  : 0 occurrences of Exception\n    ss -ltn     : 127.0.0.1:5900 and [::1]:5900 LISTEN  (loopback only)\n    hyprctl     : 0 RimWorldLinux windows  \u003c- genuinely detached\n\nBoth display modes are now demonstrated and script-flagged, so all three\nacceptance criteria are met.\n\n\n`--vnc` gave an Xvfb with nothing listening on 5900. x11vnc 0.9.17 tests for\n`WAYLAND_DISPLAY`'s PRESENCE, not its value — launched from a Wayland session it\nprints \"Wayland display server detected ... Exiting.\" and dies before binding,\nand `-quiet` swallows the message, so the symptom is a silent absence. The\nlauncher set `WAYLAND_DISPLAY=`, which clears the value but leaves the variable\ndefined. Fixed with `env -u` for x11vnc and a subshell `unset` for the game (a\nshell function cannot go through `env -u`). The game had been surviving the same\ntrap only because SDL falls back to X11 when the Wayland connect fails.\n\nThis is exactly the class of thing that only executing an acceptance line finds.\nWorth noting that the spike could not have found it — the packages did not\nexist while it ran.\n\n\nFollow-on from my 57263e7. Repointing `Mods/AutoRimmer` at the repo root meant\nthe link always resolved (the repo always exists), which dropped an About-less\nfolder into the bench's Mods/. This bench holds a zero-red-errors invariant and\nRimWorld logs mod folders it cannot read, so the link is now guarded on\n`About/About.xml` and prints \"skipped ... spec 1.1 creates it\" until then.\nProfile is back to 32 mods, 0 missing.\n\n\n- FINDINGS section 8 rewritten from PENDING to verified (cc420dc), including\n  what the fallback costs: software rendering holds the frame rate below the\n  mangohud cap, so the sim runs **50.9 tps under Xvfb where the live session\n  gives 60**, and boot takes 73s against 39s. Section 6's tps table is a\n  GPU-backed-session table; spec 1.3 should read it that way.\n- DESIGN.md updated (4cf191a) with the confirmed modlist and the spike's\n  load-bearing decisions — its own-mods list had omitted Guests and\n  RegisterLanes while the visitor-cluster line justified the cluster as existing\n  to serve them.\n\nWave 0 is closed. Every wave 1-3 spec that FINDINGS touches has its amendment.","files":null}]}